"Be careful: the floor is slippery after it rains.": "cd9b830c19ea",
"Earth rotates once every day.": "3d1a06dc7b90",
"Gymnasts are very flexible and can touch their toes easily.": "3d8b6372f456",
"Inside a moving joint, the ends of the bones never grind against each other. Each end is covered with cartilage, a smooth, rubbery layer that is more slippery than ice sliding on ice. The whole joint is wrapped in a capsule filled with a little slippery liquid called synovial fluid, which works like oil in a machine. Strong straps called ligaments hold the bones together, so they can move without coming apart.": "4839ebcc1b56",
"Joints stay healthy when you use them. Moving squeezes fluid in and out of the cartilage, which keeps it fed, and strong muscles around a joint help protect it. Warm up before sports, and never force a joint past where it wants to go. And the popping sound when someone cracks their knuckles? It is a tiny gas bubble forming in the joint fluid. Now make a simple tool to measure how far your own joints can bend.": "701b74294afe",
"Not every joint moves. The bones of your skull are joined by wavy seams called sutures, which lock them together like puzzle pieces to protect your brain. A newborn baby's skull still has soft spots between the bones so that the head can grow, but they close by about the age of two. The joints between the bones of your spine move only a little each, but together they let you bend and twist. The joints that move the most are in your arms and legs.": "79b19b0283f0",
"Plug the lamp into the socket on the wall.": "91db383e00b8",
"She hurt a ligament in her ankle during the game.": "96216a51f1a9",
"The door squeaks because its hinge needs oil.": "967bb85931f7",
"The shape of a joint decides how it moves. Your knee and elbow are hinge joints: like a door, they swing one way and back. Your shoulder and hip are ball-and-socket joints: a round ball at the top of the arm or thigh bone sits in a cup, so the limb can swing forward, backward, out to the side, and even in a circle. At the top of your neck, a pivot joint lets your head turn to say “no.” And at the base of your thumb is a saddle joint, which rocks two ways and lets your thumb touch the tip of every other finger.": "57726385288e",
"The tip of your nose is made of cartilage, not bone.": "1c83801f7b6e",
"There is always a trade-off between freedom and strength. Your shoulder has a shallow cup, which gives it the widest range of any joint in the body, but it is also the large joint that most often slips out of place. Your hip has a deep cup that holds the ball tightly. It cannot move as freely, but it can carry your whole weight when you run and jump. Your knee, the largest joint in the body, has two rubbery cushions inside and several strong ligaments to keep it steady.": "9fadea77ebf7",
"This shop sells a wide range of fruit.": "adfcc9cb5122",
"Try walking across the room without bending your knees. You will waddle like a penguin. Now try eating lunch without bending your elbows. Every time you move, bones change their angle at places where two bones meet. These places are called joints, and your body has several hundred of them, from your jaw to your smallest toe.": "c77c0cca16dc",
